{"id": "unknown-2026-09-20-004", "date": "2026-09-20", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 9, "week": 38, "weekday": "Sun"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "India’s trade deals creating new markets for entrepreneurs, says Modi", "content": "Prime Minister Narendra Modi distributed more than 51,000 appointment letters to new recruits in Government of India organisations at the 20th Rozgar Mela. \nHe linked youth employment to FTAs with about 40 countries, BRICS channels, start-ups and MSME cooperation. \nFor manufacturers and sourcing teams, the speech signals focus on skilling, apprenticeships, ITI upgrades and ease of doing", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/india-s-trade-deals-creating-new-markets-for-entrepreneurs-says-modi-313623-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-09-20-005", "date": "2026-09-20", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 9, "week": 38, "weekday": "Sun"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "CITI seeks India-US talks over 100% tariff law signed by Trump", "content": "India’s CITI has warned that possible US tariffs under the Lindsey O. Graham Sanctioning Russia and Iran Act of 2026 could affect textile and apparel exports. \nThe body said MSME-led exporters may struggle to absorb extra duties in the US, their largest market. \nIt urged closer India-US engagement, a balanced trade deal and cautioned that FTAs cannot quickly replace US demand. ", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/citi-seeks-india-us-talks-over-100-tariff-law-signed-by-trump-313621-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-09-20-006", "date": "2026-09-20", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 9, "week": 38, "weekday": "Sun"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "negative", "score": -0.5, "keywords": ["delay"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Beyond power cuts: What’s at stake for Bangladesh’s RMG sector?", "content": "BKMEA survey shows Bangladesh knitwear factories face severe energy disruption, with 90 per cent citing electricity shortages and 75 per cent hit by gas crisis. \nKnitting output fell around 37–38 per cent, sewing about 40 per cent and dyeing 51 per cent; 87 per cent reported shipment delays. \nHigher fuel costs, buyer discounts, order cuts and loan-default risks are also rising. ", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_apparel", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/apparel-news/beyond-power-cuts-what-s-at-stake-for-bangladesh-s-rmg-sector--313622-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-09-20-007", "date": "2026-09-20", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 9, "week": 38, "weekday": "Sun"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["sustainable_textile", "supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "negative", "score": -0.5, "keywords": ["delay"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Vietnam targets $48 billion textile-garment exports in 2026", "content": "Vietnam targets about $48 billion in textile-garment exports in 2026; eight-month shipments rose 2.9 per cent YoY to nearly $31.7 billion. \nExporters face a 12.5 per cent US tariff, higher costs, fabric delays and uneven order cover for the final months. \nFirms are prioritising higher-value orders, market diversification, digitalisation, input control and ESG compliance. ", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_apparel", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/apparel-news/vietnam-targets-48-billion-textile-garment-exports-in-2026-313619-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
